Peak in snowy conditions. Brimming with confidence, she dismissed warnings from locals and her guide, Carlyle Lamb, about the rapid shift toward volatile autumn mountain weather.\n\nThe pair pushed forward via the Keyhole Route. As they neared the top, a fierce alpine blizzard blew in, cloaking the peak. Though warned that the storm would completely block any scenic reward at the summit, Carrie single-mindedly refused to turn back.\n\nThey reached the top, but the descent proved fatal:\n\n* Severe Exhaustion: The numbing cold and physical exertion drained Carrie's strength. On the way down, she began collapsing, forcing her young guide to physically support her weight.\n* The Abandonment: Just below the Keyhole, Carrie became completely paralyzed by exhaustion and hypothermia, unable to move. Realizing they were trapped, Lamb wrapped her as warmly as possible and made the grueling decision to hike down the mountain on foot to get rescue help from his father.\n* A Lonely End: By the time a rescue party fought their way back up through the raging blizzard, Carrie had tragically died alone. Evidence suggested she had succumbed shortly after a minor fall while trying to desperately crawl from the spot where she was left."}]